Hoisted the profile pointer into a local and marked the invalid path as unlikely, letting the compiler keep the valid lookup as the fall-through fast path with less branch overhead.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    auto p = profile;
    if (__builtin_expect((p == NULL) || (profileIndex >= p->numFields), 0))
        return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
    return p->fields[profileIndex].num;
}
```